WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.110
(crowd cheering)
- All right, as always,

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.700
let's finish up with one last story

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:03.900
we hope will brighten your day.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.040
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.288
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.288 --> 00:00:08.670
(cheers and applause)

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.860
At 28, our next guest is already

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.500
a successful entrepreneur,
whose product is sold

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.870
at major retailers, including Target.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.250
She's created a line of dolls,

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.620
that not only reflect
a range of skin colors,

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.690
eye shapes, and face shapes,

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.880
they have natural hair for kids to style.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.140
It's called Healthy Roots,

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.910
and we have the Mastermind behind them

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:31.260
on the line right, now
watching on NBC 10 WJAR.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.240
What's up, Yelitsa?

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:33.337
How you doing?

00:00:33.337 --> 00:00:34.800
(cheers and applause)

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.660
- I'm good. How are you?

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.493
- So, I have to say,

00:00:37.493 --> 00:00:40.053
this all started as a
school project, right?

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.380
- Yeah. So, while I was
studying illustration

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:44.670
at the Rhode Island School of Design,

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.780
I was tasked with

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.670
redesigning a fairytale character.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.160
I ultimately chose Rapunzel and turned her

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.440
into a little brown girl
with kinky, curly hair,

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.660
so that I could show
other little brown girls

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.280
we can be princesses, too.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.817
From there, my classmates were telling me,

00:00:57.817 --> 00:00:59.010
"Wow, this looks like a doll."

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.960
And, I hadn't really
thought of it that way,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.670
but then I went on Facebook and talked

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:03.667
to my friends and realized,

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:05.490
"Wow, we didn't really have dolls

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:06.990
that looked like us growing up."

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:09.480
And, I saw an opportunity to do more

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:10.890
than just paint a doll brown,

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:12.960
but create an educational
hair play experience

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.970
for little Black girls, so that they know

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.230
that their natural hair is gorgeous.

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:19.680
So, from class project to
$50,000 in crowdfunding,

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.273
and then raising $1.2 million,

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.000
we now have a product line that represents

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.680
the diversity that I
didn't have growing up,

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:28.200
and shows it on toy shelves
at stores like Target.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.340
- That's incredible that this

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.810
came out of an assignment.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:32.370
So, they're not just dolls,

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:33.390
like, this is something that

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:34.800
kids can interact with, right?

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.690
That's the important
thing, as well, right?

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:39.570
- Exactly. It's-- hair is so important.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:40.620
I think people was like, "It's just hair."

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.260
It's like, "No, it's an
experience for people."

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.000
I never had products like this growing up,

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.100
and not being able to do my hair

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.050
until I was 20 years old is crazy.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.430
So, why not design something

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.770
that helps little girls
learn to love their hair

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:53.760
just the way that it is?

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:54.870
So, here's a doll that

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.130
with hair you can wash and style,

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:58.170
learn how to use shampoo, conditioner,

00:01:58.170 --> 00:01:59.790
box braids, Bantu knots,

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:01.110
all the beautiful things that

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:03.780
our natural hair can do
that we should celebrate.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:06.720
This is what this doll
is designed to show them.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:07.650
- I love it.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:10.140
Thank you so much, Yelitsa.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:12.952
I'm liking your post right now, all right?

00:02:12.952 --> 00:02:15.630
(ding)

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:16.463
Oh, my gosh.

00:02:16.463 --> 00:02:17.296
The dolls are so cute.

00:02:17.296 --> 00:02:19.650
All right, so we've hit
the time when we usually

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:20.940
give our guest a thousand dollars

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.500
courtesy of our season-long partner

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.150
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.610
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:29.160
But, since Yelitsa, well,
she's doing all right.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:29.993
She's got food in her pan.

00:02:29.993 --> 00:02:30.930
She's doing all right.

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:33.270
We're gonna give it to
someone in the audience.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:35.113
So, look under your seat.

00:02:35.113 --> 00:02:36.470
(audience cheers)

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:37.613
Look under your seats,

00:02:37.613 --> 00:02:41.071
and there's a check that's
taped under your seat.

00:02:41.071 --> 00:02:42.630
(drum roll)

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.013
Where is it? Where is it?

00:02:45.661 --> 00:02:46.650
(excited music)

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:47.501
Yes!

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:50.748
(crowd cheering)

00:02:50.748 --> 00:02:52.081
Hello! Stand up.

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:54.269
What's your name?

00:02:54.269 --> 00:02:55.669
- Suzanne Fernando.

00:02:55.669 --> 00:02:56.608
- Did you say Suzanne?

00:02:56.608 --> 00:02:57.441
- Yes.

00:02:57.441 --> 00:02:58.274
- Suzanne, what are you gonna do

00:02:58.274 --> 00:02:59.850
with that thousand dollahs?

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:01.431
- Wow. Maybe go on another vacation.

00:03:01.431 --> 00:03:02.610
(laughs)

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:03.443
- Oh, my God.

00:03:03.443 --> 00:03:05.100
Thank you for not
saying, "Just pay bills."

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:05.933
That's awesome.

00:03:05.933 --> 00:03:06.766
- Thank you!

00:03:06.766 --> 00:03:07.768
- That's so awesome.

00:03:07.768 --> 00:03:09.050
Have so much fun.

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:10.487
- Thank you so much.

00:03:10.487 --> 00:03:13.050
- Okay. Thank you to all our guests today

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:16.559
Catherine Zeta-Jones, Matt
Iseman, Lisette Olivera,

00:03:16.559 --> 00:03:18.630
Danielle Kartes, and Lawrence Zarian.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:19.836
Y'all have a great day, and if it's not,

00:03:19.836 --> 00:03:22.230
well, try and change it.

